# spinnerdemo: the Spinner widget (line preset, 100ms fps) driving Tea v2's
# tick re-arm under a real pty.
# Frame trace (each repaint is ONE write; first paint hides the cursor;
# repaints address rows ABSOLUTELY — \e[1;1H + \e[2K + char, no trailing
# \r\n):
#   resize probe (sync)  \e[?25l\e[2K|\r\n
#   tick 1 (sleep 100)   \e[1;1H\e[2K/
#   tick 2 (re-armed)    \e[1;1H\e[2K-
#   'q'                  \e[?25h + exit 0  (TaskQuit scan; the pending sleep
#                         is dropped by the quit latch)
# Frames cycle | / - \ every ~100ms, so needles span a frame BOUNDARY (the
# first-paint tail \r\n -> tick 1's \e[1;1H, then char -> \e[1;1H directly —
# repaints emit no trailing \r\n): such a substring
# cannot exist until the NEXT frame is actually written, making every expect
# deterministic regardless of tick timing (R4: never assert tick counts).
expect \e[?25l
expect |\r\n\e[1;1H\e[2K/
expect /\e[1;1H\e[2K-
send q
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
